{"text":"Because the automatic assumption is that a Nigerian female walking into a hotel alone is a sex walker. And by the way, why do these hotels focus on the ostensible supply, rather than the demand for sex walkers? In Lagos, I cannot go alone into many reputable bars and clubs. They just don't let you in if you're a woman alone. You have to be accompanied by a man. Each time I walk into a Nigerian restaurant with a man, the waiter greets the man and ignores me. The waiters are products. And there's some women who are like, yes. The waiters are products of a society that has taught them that men are more important than women. And I know the waiters don't intend any harm, but it is one thing to know intellectually and quite another to feel it emotionally. Each time they ignore me, I feel invisible. I feel upset. I want to tell them that I am just as human as the man, that I am just as worthy of that acknowledgement. These are little things, but sometimes it's the little things that sting the most.","words":[{"text":"Because","start":0.0,"end":0.94},{"text":"the","start":0.94,"end":1.1},{"text":"automatic","start":1.1,"end":1.52},{"text":"assumption","start":1.52,"end":1.9},{"text":"is","start":1.9,"end":2.14},{"text":"that","start":2.14,"end":2.22},{"text":"a","start":2.22,"end":2.32},{"text":"Nigerian","start":2.32,"end":2.58},{"text":"female","start":2.58,"end":3.06},{"text":"walking","start":3.06,"end":3.36},{"text":"into","start":3.36,"end":3.6},{"text":"a","start":3.6,"end":3.66},{"text":"hotel","start":3.66,"end":3.9},{"text":"alone","start":3.9,"end":4.18},{"text":"is","start":4.18,"end":4.36},{"text":"a","start":4.36,"end":4.5},{"text":"sex","start":4.5,"end":4.68},{"text":"walker","start":4.68,"end":5.42,"punct":"."},{"text":"And","start":7.82,"end":7.9},{"text":"by","start":7.9,"end":8.04},{"text":"the","start":8.04,"end":8.16},{"text":"way","start":8.16,"end":8.3,"punct":","},{"text":"why","start":8.44,"end":8.5},{"text":"do","start":8.5,"end":8.66},{"